  "description": "Dear Dr. Alice Smith,\n\nWe have received your submission for patient\u2011001, John Doe (male, human\u202f(NCBITaxon:9606)), whose clinical onset is recorded under HP:0001250. The case includes a documented inheritance mode of HP:0000006 and a single disorder entry (MIM:123456). Phenotypically, the patient shows the feature HP:0004322 (observed\u202f=\u202fyes) with an age of onset noted as HP:0001156. Genomic analysis identified a heterozygous missense variant (zygosity\u202f=\u202f1) in gene HGNC:5: on the GRCh38 assembly, chromosome\u202f7, positions\u202f140,453,136\u2011140,453,137, where the reference base A is replaced by G (SO:0001583, missense_variant). The case was flagged as a test case (test\u202f=\u202ftrue). All contact information is as follows: Dr. Alice Smith, Genomics Institute, https://genomics.example.org/contact/alice.\n\nOur matchmaker service returned a single highly similar patient, patient\u2011002 (Jane Smith, female, human\u202f(NCBITaxon:9606)), with a similarity score of 0.92. Jane\u2019s record lists the same onset term HP:0001156 and the same inheritance mode HP:0000006, and she is associated with disorder Orphanet:12345. Her phenotype includes the identical observed feature HP:0004322 (observed\u202f=\u202fyes). The genomic feature reported is a homozygous nonsense variant (zygosity\u202f=\u202f2) in gene HGNC:7: on the GRCh38 assembly, chromosome\u202f12, start position\u202f12,345,678, where the reference base G is changed to A (SO:0001627, nonsense_variant). This case is not a test case (test\u202f=\u202ffalse). Contact for the matching case: Dr. Bob Lee, Medical Genetics Center, https://medgen.example.org/contact/bob."
